      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>XVIII. Gif mon oðres monnes munuce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.27"/> feoh oðfæste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.28"/> butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.29"/> ðæs munuces hlafordes lefnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.30"/>, ⁊ hit him losige, þolige his se ðe hit ǽr ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>XVIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.2"/> oþres mannes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.11"/> munuce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.12"/> buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.2"/> (his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.11"/>) hlafordes leafe feoh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.3"/> befæste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.14"/>, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.2"/> hit him losie, ðolige his se ðe hit ær ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe munecan heore feoh befæstað. Gyf mon oðres monnes muneke feoh befæste buton þæs munekes hlafordes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.star"/> hleafe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.3-2"/>, ⁊ hit him losige, þolie his se ðe hit ær ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="61" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.24"/> quis alterius monacho<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.25"/> pecuniam commendauerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.26"/> sine licentia domini ipsius monachi, et ammittatur, nichil inde recipiat qui commisit ei.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_20.lnote.oe.19"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be þam þe munecan heore feoh befæstað.] Gif mon oðres monnes munuce feoh oðfæste<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Af_20.attnote.fn.3"/> butan<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Af_20.attnote.fn.4"/> ðæs munuces hlafordes<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Af_20.attnote.fn.5"/> lefnesse<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Af_20.attnote.fn.6"/>, ⁊ hit him losige, þolige his se ðe hit ǽr ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="24" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="314" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XVIII} Gif mon oðres monnes munuce feoh oðfæste butan ðæs munuces hlafordes lefnesse, ⁊ hit him losige, þolige his se ðe hit ǽr ahte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_20.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="61" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand Werthgut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_20.lnote.de.2"/> dem Mönche eines anderen Mannes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_20.lnote.de.3"/> anvertraut, ohne Erlaubniss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_20.lnote.de.4"/> des Herrn des Mönches, und es jenem verloren geht, so trage dessen Verlust<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_20.lnote.de.5"/> wer es früher besessen hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone entrusts valuables to another man’s monk without the permission of the monk’s lord, and it is lost to him, let the one who owned it before bear its loss.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="75" ed="#attenborough"/>If property is entrusted to a monk in the service of another man without the permission of the monk’s lord, and he loses it, its former owner shall bear the loss.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone entrusts property to another man’s monk, without the permission of the monk’s lord, and it is lost to him, he who owned it before is to bear its loss.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="315" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone entrusts property to another man’s monk without the permission of the monk’s lord, and it is lost from him, let him who owned it before forfeit it.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="282"><label>possibly derived from</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-28">Af El 28</ref> <quote>Af 20 (if not Af Int 28)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="315"><label>shared vocabulary</label> <ref target="clause:Af_8">Af 8</ref> <quote>This term appears elsewhere only in the Mercian-influenced Old English translation of Bede and §9</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="303"><ref target="clause:Af_8">Af 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="404"><ref target="clause:InCn_Inscr">In Cn</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">munuc <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">munuc So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">befæst <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">befæst Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">leofn. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> leafe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">leofn. So; leafe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ó <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ó altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> u <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second u on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">be <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">be on an erasure</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The note number is printed 14 in the text, but the footnote that belongs here is no. 13 (‘be auf Rasur’); there is no footnote 14 on the page.</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inde <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> Si q. a. pec. <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inde instead of Si q. a. pec. Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. m. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. m. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-uit <hi rend="italic">R T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-uit R T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">unterstrichen und</hi> aldres <hi rend="italic">später übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">underlined, and aldres written above later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Neben den Mönch (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 6) stellt Unfreie und Unmündige als unverantwortlich hin für das ihnen Anvertraute (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4) Hn 23, 3. 45, 2f, der Q benutzt. <hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> mündig 13. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Pol Mai I 417</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn 23, 3. 45, 2f, which uses Q, places unfree persons and minors alongside the monk (<hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> 6) as not answerable for what has been entrusted to them (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4). <hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> mündig 13. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Pol Mai I 417</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Vieh’ zu eng; <hi rend="italic">losian</hi> kann auch ‘verloren gehn’ neben ‘entlaufen’ heissen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘cattle’ is too narrow; <hi rend="italic">losian</hi> can mean ‘be lost’ as well as ‘run away’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Kirchenherr 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Kirchenherr 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hb modernisiert, und B setzt anlautend <hi rend="italic">h-</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi> 1a <hi rend="italic">β</hi>) unorganisch davor</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hb modernises, and B prefixes an inorganic initial <hi rend="italic">h-</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> 1a <hi rend="italic">β</hi>)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_20.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘empfange nicht zurückersetzt’ Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘let him not receive it back made good’ Q</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_20.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>oðfæste</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">befæste</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_20.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>butan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">buton (his) hlafordes leafe feoh befæste</hi>. H*.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_20.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>hlafordes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Underlined in B, and <hi rend="italic">aldres</hi> written above, later.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_20.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>lefnesse</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hleafe</hi>. B.</seg></note>
